{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01872",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 8.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "So, hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.74,
      "end_seconds": 13.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.15,
      "end_seconds": 20.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "I'm here because of pain under my right ribs after fatty meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.39,
      "end_seconds": 24.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.37,
      "end_seconds": 40.64,
      "duration_seconds": 14.27,
      "text": "Let me think, probably about two weeks. Yeah. I didn't want to bother you but it it keeps coming back. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.74,
      "end_seconds": 51.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.75,
      "end_seconds": 79.06,
      "duration_seconds": 25.31,
      "text": "Hmm, only lying still, and it's not much. I'd say all the time. Moderate, really. Yes, fatty meals. That makes it worse. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. Right, I've had bloating too, for one week. With bloating, severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.76,
      "end_seconds": 93.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "okay, a few quick ones: dark urine, fever, yellow eyes or pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.95,
      "end_seconds": 105.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "let me think, no dark urine, fever, yellow eyes or pale stools, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.4,
      "end_seconds": 108.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Ah. Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.81,
      "end_seconds": 111.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "no problems with breathing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.41,
      "end_seconds": 116.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.52,
      "end_seconds": 123.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Just a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.25,
      "end_seconds": 141.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "So, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.39,
      "end_seconds": 144.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "I've got asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.66,
      "end_seconds": 147.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.66,
      "end_seconds": 156.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. An antacid. I take it 10 ml, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.2,
      "end_seconds": 159.16,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.67,
      "end_seconds": 165.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.87,
      "end_seconds": 168.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.59,
      "end_seconds": 173.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.41,
      "end_seconds": 181.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.81,
      "end_seconds": 189.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.52,
      "end_seconds": 192.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.52,
      "end_seconds": 200.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.01,
      "end_seconds": 205.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.44,
      "end_seconds": 210.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.4,
      "end_seconds": 218.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.77,
      "end_seconds": 233.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "that's it, just a little longer.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.24,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.41,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 128 over 70, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 36.6 degrees, pulse is 64 beats a a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.05,
      "end_seconds": 256.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.8,
      "end_seconds": 260.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.27,
      "end_seconds": 265.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.25,
      "end_seconds": 268.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.85,
      "end_seconds": 289.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "It is tender under the right ribs and you stop breathing in when I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.23,
      "end_seconds": 296.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.5,
      "end_seconds": 333.54,
      "duration_seconds": 28.04,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I don't have a clear answer today: gallstone-related pain is possible, and so is a stomach ulcer. I think an ultrasound of the abdomen makes sense here, for biliary pain. I'm going to to order liver blood tests, for biliary pain. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.9,
      "end_seconds": 360.88,
      "duration_seconds": 24.98,
      "text": "I'm prescribing paracetamol, 1 gram, four times a day when needed, one week. You take it by mouth. It's for pain. Avoid fatty and fried foods until the scan. I'd like you to see the surgical clinic as well, and I'll write the referral. Please come and see me after the scan. Right, that's the plan. Do you wanna ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.53,
      "end_seconds": 364.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.57,
      "end_seconds": 371.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}